{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Internal engine for dev.git.{read,write,remote_op}: probes git availability once per process (cached PATH scan - a git-less box gets a plain 'git is not installed' err, never a spawn failure), resolves the repo name in runtime/dev/repos.json, enforces the per-mode verb allowlist, builds argv (git --no-optional-locks -C <path> <verb> <args...>), and makes ONE spawn - no shell, nothing interpolated. The exit status is honored: a nonzero git exit answers status err with `code` and the first fatal:/error:/CONFLICT line as msg, so compound commands and the panel can trust status (system_call reported every exit as ok, which hid every git failure behind stderr). Adds a neutral commit identity when the repo has none; pull defaults to --ff-only unless a strategy flag is stated; write mode includes clean (abandon's discard). Call the mode wrappers, not this.","import":"use flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse ndata::data::Data;","params":[{"name":"repo","type":"String"},{"name":"verb","type":"String"},{"name":"args","type":"JSONArray"},{"name":"mode","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"nqypsj1a02428c568n8","readers":[],"time":1788639910561,"username":"system","writers":[]}